    "wikipedia_summary": "<i><b>Aloe affinis</b></i> is a species of aloe plant, endemic to Limpopo, Gauteng, and Mpumalanga, of South Africa. It grows 200–300 mm tall excluding inflorescence, with 16-20 leaves per plant, each leaf being roughly 200 mm long x 50–100 mm wide.",
